description:
Harden creature attack and action parsing so no printed attack, damage value, or
range is dropped, and alternate modes are represented as alternatives.

Root cause: brittle regex parsing over stat-block prose. Each of the listed
defects is a different failure of the same parser, which is why A2's shared
normalization is a prerequisite.

Required membership — all of:
- alternate damage modes and swarm thresholds (full-health vs half-health swarm
  damage);
- attacks missing because the bonus appears as a parenthetical alternate;
- Unicode-minus damage silently dropped;
- the swallowed Wererat Hand Crossbow action (shared with B2);
- nonstandard and single-value ranges;
- uniform flat vs dice damage field shapes (shared with B3);
- target qualifiers currently truncated;
- full attack inventory and action-boundary regression across all 317 creatures.

Closes findings: F-27, F-28, F-29, F-30, F-31, F-34, F-35, SOL-006, CAP-004,
Fable F3.
